{
  "_about": [
    "THE DTYPE SEAM ABI -- the single declaration both lanes are checked against.",
    "",
    "Four conventions sit between tinybendygrad/runtime/dtype.c and",
    "tinybendygrad/runtime/dtype.js.  Two of them have already shipped a silent",
    "bug.  A comment did not prevent either: both lanes were written by reading",
    "each other's CODE, which is the thing under dispute.  So this file is not",
    "prose -- abi_gate.py reads it, drives both lanes, and attributes every",
    "disagreement to one of these four ids.",
    "",
    "`site` entries are [file, line, token].  The gate checks that the cited line",
    "still contains the token.  That is a DANGLING-POINTER check, not a",
    "behaviour check: it can tell you this document has gone stale, and it can",
    "NOT tell you a lane conforms.  Conformance is measured, in `rows`.",
    "",
    "Generated-file sites (`probe.gen.c`, `probe.js`) are the BEND BACKENDS, not",
    "the lanes.  They are cited because two of the four conventions are actually",
    "implemented there and only inherited by the lanes."
  ],
  "backend": {
    "c": {
      "file": "gen/probe.gen.c",
      "dispatch": [
        {
          "body": "io_exec",
          "token": "io_eff_rows[c].run(e, fs, w)"
        }
      ],
      "note": "the frame is Term* fs of n = cid_arity(c) slots; ctr_take at :3136 built it"
    },
    "js": {
      "file": "gen/probe.js",
      "dispatch": [
        {
          "body": "io_run",
          "token": "op.run(...op.args, op.kont)"
        }
      ],
      "note": "op.args is a JS array of NATIVE values, passed through with NO conversion"
    },
    "_cite": "GENERATED FILES ARE CITED BY BODY NAME, NEVER BY file:line. `bend -o` embeds `import \"./x.js\"` verbatim, so editing a lane moves every probe.js body line: measured here, editing dtype.js moved all of them by exactly +21 (894 -> 915 lines) and changed no convention."
  },
  "abi": [
    {
      "id": "ABI-1",
      "name": "flat frame, arity is a property of the CID",
      "statement": [
        "A seam receives its arguments as a POSITIONAL frame whose length is",
        "cid_arity(the CID).  `f[i]` is argument i.  An H.I64 argument is ONE",
        "slot, not two -- it is a constructor node that the lane must OPEN.",
        "Arity is declared once, in dtype.bend's signature, and both lanes must",
        "consume exactly that many arguments."
      ],
      "shipped_bug": {
        "was": "static s64 i64_of(Term* f) { return (s64)(((u64)(u32)f[0] << 32) | (u32)f[1]); }",
        "did": "read f[0],f[1] of the ENCLOSING frame, i.e. arg0 + arg1, for a 1-argument seam",
        "answered": "two allocation addresses, which are plausible pointers",
        "fixed_at": "tinybendygrad/runtime/dtype.c:205",
        "patch": ".agents/slop/w64mile/dtype-c-i64.patch:7-13"
      },
      "declared_arity": {
        "_source": "tinybendygrad/dtype.bend:576-614",
        "Dt.bf16": 1,
        "Dt.fp16": 1,
        "Dt.fp8_from": 2,
        "Dt.fp8_to": 2,
        "Dt.i64_trunc": 1,
        "Dt.i64_floor_div": 2,
        "Dt.i64_floor_mod": 2,
