        "abi123_trunc_A",
        "abi123_trunc_B",
        "abi123_fdiv_b3",
        "abi123_fdiv_b5",
        "abi123_fdiv_b1"
      ],
      "predicate": [
        "ARITY-2 LIVENESS: the three abi123_fdiv_* rows vary ONLY the second",
        "argument, over three values with three distinct CPython answers.  A lane",
        "that consumed fewer than 2 arguments returns the same answer for all",
        "three.  Three distinct answers is the only passing count.",
        "ARITY-1: abi123_trunc_* is the identity on one record, so any frame",
        "misread -- over or under -- moves it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ABI-2",
      "name": "a record crosses BY FIELD NAME, and the names are hi/lo",
      "statement": [
        "An H.I64 crosses the JS boundary as a JS OBJECT carrying its BEND FIELD",
        "NAMES, {hi, lo}.  It never crosses as positional fst/snd.  There is no",
        "name at all on the C side: a record is a constructor node and is opened",
        "POSITIONALLY by ctr_take.  So `p.fst`/`p.snd` and `a[0]`/`a[1]` are BOTH",
        "wrong, in opposite directions, under the same one CID with the same name.",
        "The names are load-bearing because they are the only thing the two",
        "representations share."
      ],
      "shipped_bug": {
        "was": "function i64_of(p) { ... p.fst >>> 0 ... p.snd >>> 0 ... }",
        "did": "read two fields that do not exist on the incoming object",
        "answered": "0 for every input: undefined >>> 0 === 0",
        "consequence": "Dt.i64_trunc, the IDENTITY, is not the identity.  0/30 rows.",
        "fixed_at": "tinybendygrad/runtime/dtype.js:160 (inbound) and :168 (outbound).  i64_of reads p.hi/p.lo; pack64 answers {$:\"tinybendygrad/helpers.I64\", hi, lo}.  ABID `js-repair-abi2`'s DIAGNOSTIC edit is now the shipped text, which is the check that the obligation was applied and not merely stated."
      },
