      "predicate": [
        "Same decision procedure as ABI-2; this is the branch that says SWAPPED.",
        "Every abi123_* row has hi != lo BY CONSTRUCTION, because when hi == lo the",
        "order is unobservable and the row could not fail.  That is a theorem about",
        "the fixture set, not an assumption: the gate prints both words per row."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ABI-4",
      "name": "scalar transport: an F32 crosses as its BIT PATTERN",
      "statement": [
        "A U32 crosses as itself in both lanes.  An F32 crosses as its 32-bit",
        "PATTERN in C and as its VALUE under node, and each lane must undo that",
        "on the way in and NOT undo it on the way out.  Concretely:",
        "  C   : the frame slot IS the pattern.  Read it with (u32)f[i].  Answer a",
        "        pattern.  No conversion anywhere.",
        "  node: op.args carries the VALUE (bend's JS book emits 1.5, not",
        "        0x3FC00000) and f32_show() consumes the raw RESULT as a value, so",
        "        the JS lane must answer a VALUE.",
        "WHICH HELPER OWINS WHICH IS NOT A CHOICE.  `of32` is PATTERN->VALUE and",
        "belongs on an ANSWER; `bits32` is VALUE->PATTERN and belongs on an",
        "ARGUMENT.  Once each, at the seam, never in the other place.  And which",
        "direction a seam owes is `dtype.bend`'s SIGNATURE, not the lane's habit:",
        "  Dt.fp16(x: F32) -> IO(F32)          value in AND value out",
        "  Dt.bf16(bits: U32) -> IO(F32)       pattern in, value out",
        "  Dt.fp8_to(bits, kind) -> IO(F32)    pattern in, value out",
        "  Dt.fp8_from(bits, kind) -> IO(U32)  pattern in and out; crosses no value"
      ],
      "shipped_bug": {
        "was": "THREE sites, not one: dtype_fp16 applied of32 to its own F32 ARGUMENT; fp8_decode applied of32 to an arithmetic VALUE and so converted twice; dtype_fp8_to answered a PATTERN where its declared return type is F32",
        "did": "of32(1.5) is 1.4e-45, the smallest f32 subnormal, and of32(1073741824) is 2.0",
        "answered": "fp16(1.5) printed 0, fp16(1073741824) printed 2, fp8_to(0x3C) printed 1, and fp8_to(0x7F,e5m2) printed 2143289300 -- which is the PATTERN 0x7FC00000, f32 nan, read as a value",
        "second_site": "dtype.js's own return-style split: dtype_bf16 and dtype_fp16 answer of32 (a value) while fp8_decode answered bits32 (a pattern)",
        "consequence": "Dt.i64_trunc and the five abi123_* rows are untouched, so a gate whose other rows are U32 could call the lane repaired while 4 of 12 were wrong -- the green that was worth less than its own red",
        "fixed_at": "REPAIRED in tinybendygrad/runtime/dtype.js -- THREE lines and NO net line count: the of32 on dtype_fp16's argument deleted, the of32 inside fp8_decode deleted, one of32 added to dtype_fp8_to's return.  Shipped 57/98, repaired 98/98, measured by `.agents/slop/abi4/abi4_gate.py`."
